  "'WIKIDATA' ON THE OVERVIEW — THE KNOWLEDGE GRAPH AT ITS DATA MODEL; ITS OWN Q-NUMBERS GIVEN, ITS ROLE AS HUB OF THE NAME AUTHORITIES (ISNI, VIAF, ORCID) AND ITS PSEUDONYM PROPERTY NOT CARRIED",
  ("THE KNOWLEDGE BASE, SIGNED OUT, 2026-11-01: 'Wikidata is a free, open, and collaborative multilingual knowledge graph hosted by the Wikimedia Foundation. It serves as a central storage hub for structured data used by Wikipedia, Wikimedia sister projects, and external applications.' "
   "Key Features: CC0 ('All data is released'); 'Q-number' items ('`Q42` for Douglas Adams') and P-numbers ('`P69` for \"educated at\"'); statements and triples with references; multilingual labels, descriptions and aliases; the SPARQL Query Service. Eight cards: Wikidata (two), Wikipedia, the Query Service, GitHub, three YouTube videos."),
  "The innocent reading first. Asked for the name, the Overview introduces the knowledge base as a newcomer would meet it: host, license, how items and statements work, and how to query.",
  ["THE DATA MODEL AT ITS GRAIN. Statements 'link entities to values, often backed by references to external sources', and labels, descriptions and aliases 'exist across hundreds of languages'. The introduction: 'The Wikidata repository consists mainly of items , each one having a label , a description and any number of aliases .' and 'Wikidata records not just statements, but also their sources, and connections to other databases.' The host is right ('hosted by the Wikimedia Foundation'); Wikimedia Deutschland, the editors 'who decide on the rules of content creation and management', the bots, the launch of 29 October 2012 and the count ('more than 123 million data entities') are not carried.",
   "THE LICENSE WIDENED. 'All data is released under a Creative Commons CC0 public domain dedication'. The introduction limits it: 'All structured data from the main, Property, Lexeme, and EntitySchema namespaces is available under the Creative Commons CC0 License ; text in the other namespaces is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License'.",
   "THE HUB OF NAMES NOT CARRIED. The composition gives Wikidata's internal identifiers ('Q42', 'P69') and no external one. The census row's interest is the other kind: 'A property that links an item to an external database, such as an authority control database used by libraries and archives, is called an identifier', with 'ISNI (P213)', VIAF numbers 'incorporated into Wikidata', and 'Both Wikipedia and Wikidata include pages with ORCID identifiers' in the saved sources. The pseudonym property is absent too: 'pseudonym (P742)', 'alias used by someone', whose aliases run 'pen name stage name code name user name known professionally as heteronym nom de plume', with 'Data type String'. 'Aliases' is the composition's only word for a second name."],
  "The knowledge base composed accurately as a data model and a query service, with its license stated wider than its own page states it. The two features that make it a census row, the identifier properties that join ISNI, VIAF and ORCID, and the property that stores a heteronym as a string on its bearer's item, are absent.",
